      "Name/Label": "Institute for Developmental Philosophy",
      "Description": "For its first 10 years of operation, the Institute focused on ameliorating hyperpolarization. But since 2023, the organization has focused primarily on developing its core philosophy, which is known as developmental philosophy.\n\nDevelopmental Philosophy is an emerging body of thought that explores the deeper meanings of evolution, with a special emphasis on noosphere evolution—the evolution of human history. Developmental philosophy is an umbrella term that includes process philosophy, integral philosophy, and related philosophies that recognize the moral or spiritual significance of the universe’s ceaseless process of becoming. Its most prominent proponents include Pierre Teilhard de Chardin (1881–1955) and Alfred North Whitehead (1861–1947).\n\nThe Institute’s name change is designed to better reflect its current mission, which is to advance humanity’s understanding of noosphere evolution.",
